>>>markdown
# Dashboards

The `# dashboard` tag renders a query as a dashboard layout. Dimensions appear as headers at the top of each row, while measures display as KPI cards and nested queries render as charts or tables within cards.

The examples below use the following source:
>>>malloy
source: products is duckdb.table('../data/products.parquet') extend {
  measure:
    product_count is count()
    avg_price is retail_price.avg()
    total_retail is retail_price.sum()
    max_price is retail_price.max()
}
>>>markdown

## Basic Dashboard

Apply `# dashboard` to any query with dimensions, measures, and nested views. Dimensions become row headers, measures become KPI values, and nested queries render in cards.

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  aggregate: avg_price, total_retail, max_price
  nest: by_brand is {
    group_by: brand
    aggregate:
      avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
      product_count
    limit: 8
  }
}
>>>markdown

## Grid Layout with Columns

By default, dashboard items arrange themselves in an auto-fit grid. Use `columns` to set a fixed number of equal-width columns:

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard { columns = 3 }
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  aggregate: avg_price, total_retail, max_price
}
>>>markdown

## Span: Controlling Item Width

For precise control, use `# span` on individual items. Spans use a 12-column grid (like Bootstrap). When any item in a group has a `span`, the layout switches to the 12-column grid for that group.

Common patterns: `span = 12` (full width), `span = 6` (half), `span = 4` (third), `span = 3` (quarter).

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  aggregate:
    # span = 4
    avg_price
    # span = 4
    total_retail
    # span = 4
    max_price
  nest:
    # span = 6
    # bar_chart
    by_brand_chart is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate: avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
      limit: 8
    }
    # span = 6
    by_brand_table is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate:
        avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
        product_count
      limit: 8
    }
}
>>>markdown

## Row Breaks

Use `# break` to force items onto a new row. This is useful when you want KPIs on one row and charts/tables on the next:

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  aggregate:
    # span = 4
    avg_price
    # span = 4
    total_retail
    # span = 4
    max_price
  nest:
    # break
    # span = 6
    # bar_chart
    by_brand_chart is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate: avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
      limit: 8
    }
    # span = 6
    by_brand_table is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate:
        avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
        product_count
      limit: 8
    }
}
>>>markdown

## Subtitles

Add a subtitle to any dashboard item with `# subtitle="..."`:

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  nest:
    # span = 6
    # bar_chart
    # subtitle="Top 10 brands by average price"
    by_brand_chart is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate: avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
      limit: 10
    }
    # span = 6
    # subtitle="Top 10 brands"
    by_brand_table is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate:
        avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
        product_count
      limit: 10
    }
}
>>>markdown

## Big Value KPIs

The `# big_value` plugin renders a single measure as a prominent KPI card. When placed inside a dashboard, big values automatically center within their card and vertically align with adjacent items.

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  nest:
    # span = 6
    # big_value
    avg_price_kpi is {
      aggregate:
        # label="Average Retail Price"
        # currency
        avg_price is retail_price.avg()
    }
    # span = 6
    # bar_chart
    # subtitle="Top 10 brands"
    brand_chart is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate: avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
      limit: 10
    }
}
>>>markdown

## Big Values with Sparklines

Big values can include inline sparkline charts. Define a nested query for the trend data, mark it `# hidden`, and reference it with the `sparkline` parameter:

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  nest:
    # span = 4
    # big_value
    avg_price_card is {
      aggregate:
        # label="Avg Price"
        # currency
        # big_value { sparkline=price_trend }
        avg_price is retail_price.avg()
      # line_chart { size=spark y.independent=true }
      # hidden
      nest: price_trend is {
        group_by: product_bucket is floor(id / 100)::number
        # currency
        aggregate: price is retail_price.avg()
        order_by: product_bucket
        limit: 20
      }
    }
    # span = 4
    # big_value
    total_products_card is {
      aggregate:
        # label="Products"
        # big_value { sparkline=count_trend }
        product_count is count()
      # bar_chart { size=spark y.independent=true }
      # hidden
      nest: count_trend is {
        group_by: product_bucket is floor(id / 100)::number
        aggregate: cnt is count()
        order_by: product_bucket
        limit: 20
      }
    }
    # span = 4
    # big_value
    max_price_card is {
      aggregate:
        # label="Max Price"
        # currency
        # big_value { sparkline=max_trend }
        max_price is retail_price.max()
      # line_chart { size=spark y.independent=true }
      # hidden
      nest: max_trend is {
        group_by: product_bucket is floor(id / 100)::number
        # currency
        aggregate: price is retail_price.max()
        order_by: product_bucket
        limit: 20
      }
    }
}
>>>markdown

## Borderless Tables

By default, tables inside dashboards render inside cards with borders and shadows. Add `# borderless` to remove the card styling:

>>>malloy
#(docs) size=large limit=5000
# dashboard
run: products -> {
  group_by: category
  aggregate: avg_price, product_count
  nest:
    # borderless
    by_brand is {
      group_by: brand
      aggregate:
        avg_retail is retail_price.avg()
        product_count
      limit: 5
    }
}
>>>markdown

## Tag Reference

| Tag | Applies to | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `# dashboard` | Query/view | Renders as a dashboard layout |
| `# dashboard { columns = N }` | Query/view | Sets N equal-width columns |
| `# span = N` | Field | Sets item width (N out of 12 columns) |
| `# break` | Field | Forces a new row before this item |
| `# subtitle="..."` | Field | Adds a subtitle below the item title |
| `# borderless` | Nested table | Removes card styling from a table |
| `# big_value` | Nested query | Renders as a prominent KPI card |

